s commented for hard-to-understand areas\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-10T22:58:02Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOE6kgeQ","login":"shaurya20335","name":"Shaurya Shukla"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 5.5"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-13T16:47:40Z","messageBody":"The NVPF diffusivity data are tabulated against the positive particle\nconcentration (131 to 15,197 mol/m3), but NVPF_diffusivity_Chayambuka2022\nscaled the stoichiometry by the initial electrolyte concentration\n(1000 mol/m3), so it only read the dilute end of the table and the cathode\ndiffusivity was 20 to 50 times too large. Scale by the positive electrode\nmaximum concentration, as HC_diffusivity_Chayambuka2022 does for the negative\nelectrode, and test the values with a relative tolerance.\n\nFixes #5885\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix: look up Chayambuka2022 NVPF diffusivity at the solid concentration","oid":"63f25cfaf9ca692348ead8d5af9e975e8e3239c7"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-10T23:04:29Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOE6kgeQ","login":"shaurya20335","name":"Shaurya Shukla"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 5.5"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-13T16:47:52Z","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"add changelog entry for #5889","oid":"fa3fd0e27ec738e2b513f357c7cde22fcea5cba0"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-12T07:06:16Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"U_kgDOE6kgeQ","login":"shaurya20335","name":"Shaurya Shukla"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 5.5"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-13T16:47:53Z","messageBody":"…n notebook\n\n- Check every Chayambuka2022 function value with rel=1e-3 (abs=0), so the\n  diffusivities are actually checked, and give the expected values enough\n  digits for that tolerance. 